Title: The journal carries outer, inner and reasons, with a reader for old records
Created: 2026-09-16
Author: MinhHaDuong
Blocked-by: 0804

--- log ---
2026-09-16T07:53Z MinhHaDuong created

--- body ---

## Context

Third child of tracker 0801, and the one that goes through a one-way door.

The author ruled on 2026-09-16, choosing break-and-migrate over serialising the
two axes back into a single string: **the journal carries the outer state, the
inner state and the reason set as separate fields, and a reader maps old
records onto the new shape** so past incidents stay comparable.

That is the more honest structure and it is the more expensive one. The
alternative — keeping one field on the wire while the code carries two axes —
was rejected. Do not re-introduce it as a simplification.

## What the door opens onto

`heartbeat.phase`, `announce phase=` and `sweep-end.phase` are read by
`bench/sdt_stall_probe.py`, the phase probes, **every incident JSON under
`verification/incidents/`**, and `Zotero.SDTPackSitter.state`, which became an
external contract the day the author's live console readings went through it.

Two incidents of 2026-09-15 were reconstructed entirely from these records.
If a future reader cannot compare them against a new run, the repository loses
its only worked examples of the defect class it is built around.

## What to build

- The record's new shape, and the emitters that write it.
- **A reader that maps old records to it** — `draining` becomes
  `RUNNING/draining`, a blocked-phase string becomes
  `DEFERRED` plus that reason, and so on for every value the old vocabulary
  could hold. The mapping is the deliverable, not a detail of it.
- The consumers updated to read through it.

## Test

The control is the whole ticket: **run the new reader over the two committed
incident files of 2026-09-15 and assert the reconstruction matches what those
incidents are documented to show** — the drain plateau, `completed: 0`, the
frozen progress at 90. A reader that cannot reproduce a known past reading is
not a migration, and a test written only against synthetic new-shape records
would pass while proving nothing about the door.

Second: an old value the mapping does NOT cover must be refused loudly, not
silently defaulted — the same discipline `setPhase` gets in 0804.

## Verification

- [ ] The reader reproduces both 2026-09-15 incidents from their committed JSON
- [ ] An unmapped old value is refused, with the refusal asserted
- [ ] `Zotero.SDTPackSitter.state`'s change is written down where a console
      reader will meet it, since the author reads it by hand
- [ ] `make check` green

## Invariants

- No incident file is rewritten. They are evidence; the reader adapts to them.
- `bench/sdt_stall_probe.py` keeps working on both shapes.

## Exit criteria

The journal carries the three fields, and a reader demonstrably reconstructs
the two preserved incidents from their original records.
